</invention-title>
                <invention-title lang="en">CONTINUOUS STACKED DUAL WRAP TUBE END CLOSURE FOR ANTI-ICING SYSTEMS</invention-title>
            </bibliographic-data>
            <abstract lang="en">
                <p>A control system for an anti-icing system, comprising: a deicing boot (402); a controller (127); and a tangible, non-transitory memory configured to communicate with the controller, the tangible, non-transitory memory having instructions stored thereon that, in response to execution by the controller, cause the controller to perform operations comprising: receiving, by the controller, an enable command from a control interface; polling, by the controller, a sensor for a sensor data; receiving, by the controller, the sensor data from the sensor; passing, by the controller, the sensor data to an ice protection logic; determining, by the controller via the ice protection logic, an icing condition; and providing, by the controller, a compressed gas to the deicing boot.</p>
            </abstract>
